#
# Counter-example for the native math:IncompleteDependencyModel gate: a
# math:FactorGraph declares no math:dependencyGraph, so its bipartite
# variable/factor structure is absent and it cannot fix a joint distribution. The
# native gate MUST emit math:IncompleteDependencyModel (and no other probability
# failure class). Every other probability-layer completeness gate stays satisfied:
# no math:MarkovKernel, math:BayesianNetwork, or math:JointProbabilityTable is
# present to trip Gate 4's other arms, and no probability-model lowering or
# preservation-kind claim is declared to trip Gates 3 or 5.
# Back-reference: math:FactorGraph / math:IncompleteDependencyModel
# (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:incompleteFactorGraph a math:FactorGraph .
